/* V60 — the band you could not see, then the band that was too loud.

   V57 pays up to 4.6x for kills deep in the arena, and the design rests on the player seeing where
   that starts. Captured against a populated arena, it did not.

   The cause was a rendering mistake worth naming because it is easy to repeat: the band was drawn
   with `globalCompositeOperation='lighter'`, an additive wash, which only shows over something dark.
   Three of the four worlds put a lit skyline or a bright planet exactly where the band sits, and
   adding a few percent of light to an already-bright cityscape produces nothing the eye can find. It
   was legible in the empty test arena I checked it in and invisible in the game. Check a visual
   change against a representative background, not a convenient one.

   The first fix over-corrected. It added a dark wash above the band, two rules, tick marks down both
   edges and two text labels — to a screen already carrying a wave bar, a boss bar, a combo readout,
   two ability buttons, a weapon chip and an avatar. Play feedback was that the game does not look
   good, and that is fair: legibility was real but it was bought with clutter, and clutter is its own
   kind of unreadable.

   What is left is the part that carries the meaning. One dashed line where the payout starts, drawn
   with normal compositing so it survives a bright background, and the number — small, at the left
   edge, and only while hostiles are actually in the zone. At rest the arena carries no extra text at
   all. */

const V60={
 /* Kept as one knob in case the line needs to come back up, but the wash, the ticks and the second
    label are gone -- see the note above. */
 lineAlpha:.16
};

/* Replaces V57's own drawing wrapper rather than layering over it — two bands drawn on top of each
   other would be worse than either. V57's scoring is untouched; this is only how it is shown. */
const v60DrawBase=v57Draw;
drawReactor=function(){
 const line=v57Line();
 const top=line*V57.start;
  let live=0;
 for(const o of game.orbs)if(v57Depth(o.y)>.15)live++;
 const heat=Math.min(1,live/4);
 const world=worlds[game.world%worlds.length];

 ctx.save();

 /* Reduced after play feedback that the screen does not look good. The first version added a dark
    wash, two rules, tick marks down both edges and two text labels -- to a screen that already
    carries a wave bar, a boss bar, a combo readout, two ability buttons, a weapon chip and an
    avatar. Legibility was real but it was bought with clutter, and clutter is itself a way of being
    unreadable.

    What survives is the part that carries the meaning: one line where the payout starts, and the
    number, shown small and only while the zone is actually doing something. The dark wash, the side
    ticks and the second label are gone. */
 ctx.strokeStyle=world.accent;
 ctx.lineCap='round';
 ctx.globalAlpha=V60.lineAlpha+heat*.34;
 ctx.lineWidth=1.2;
 ctx.setLineDash([7,11]);
 ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(0,top);ctx.lineTo(W,top);ctx.stroke();
 ctx.setLineDash([]);

 /* The number fades in only when hostiles are actually in the zone. At rest the arena carries no
    extra text at all. */
 if(heat>.05){
  ctx.globalAlpha=heat*.7;
  ctx.fillStyle=world.accent;
  ctx.font=`800 ${isMobile?9:10}px system-ui`;
  ctx.textAlign='left';
  ctx.textBaseline='bottom';
  ctx.fillText(`×${V57.pay.toFixed(1)} ZONE`,10,top-4);
 }
 ctx.restore();

 v60DrawBase();
};
